<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Svear</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Suiones</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Svear were a North Germanic people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malaren">Lake Mälaren</a> region and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppland">Uppland</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, the Suiones described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>. Their kings, centred at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a>, extended their rule over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geats">Geats</a> around 1000, and Sweden takes its name from them. Rich graves at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vendel">Vendel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valsgarde">Valsgärde</a> reflect their warrior elite.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/svear.jpg" alt="Svear" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flappiefh; derivative work by rowanwindwhistler · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scandinavia-12th_century.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
